{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"mx-finance-data","displayName":"All-Market Financial Data Hub","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/financial-ai-analyst/skills/mx-finance-data","publisherHandle":"financial-ai-analyst","publisherDisplayName":"Financial AI Analyst","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/financial-ai-analyst","version":"1.0.12","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1780658980664,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/mx-finance-data/card?ownerHandle=financial-ai-analyst&version=1.0.12","sha256":"2903366bde27f85e49bbb08ec20dd33fefe15271c03deb81863f1f2b36371329","size":2285,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"8424316663e067d1652eed77ad52574734eab13041d994527dfb58edaa9c3858","bundleFingerprints":["4c67a5d7ecbd5516fb799f55ad43b1f38c697c076e29ea01422d766b8cfb13ab","f23bf6e4c3d8f82ed3937d28179459e2863986d8904fbbc21ceca954ae3de99a"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6307,"sha256":"17fbaa5eb5539680c597ef8ec6f2777a99d8e7a0d1e3a2ce4c660c2d671a6410","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/get_data.py","size":34751,"sha256":"465e331ce8c1961b00bc53558b974b39bbabc4c32e94f2eaae3c99525daec785","contentType":"text/x-python"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is a coherent finance-data query tool, but an undocumented Python endpoint override can expose the user's Eastmoney API key if invoked with an untrusted URL.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789172741716,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"API Credential Disclosure Through Unrestricted Endpoint Overrides"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/get_data.py"},"region":{"startLine":671,"endLine":729}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"7329b3cc133b24bf"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/get_data.py`, lines 671–729  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Server-Side Request Forgery / Credential Disclosure  \n**Risk Level**: Medium  \n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\nasync def query_mx_finance_data(\n        query: str,\n        indicators: Optional[str] = None,\n        output_dir: Optional[Path] = None,\n        api_base: Optional[str] = None,\n        entity_api_base: Optional[str] = None,\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    output_dir = output_dir or _get_default_output_dir()\n    output_dir = Path(output_dir)\n    output_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    url = api_base or DEFAULT_SEARCH_API_URL\n    entity_api_url = entity_api_base or DEFAULT_ENTITY_API_URL\n    result = _make_result_base(query)\n    entity_tags: Optional[List[Dict[str, Any]]] = None\n\n    try:\n        api_key = EM_API_KEY\n        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=120.0) as client:\n            recognized_tags = await _recognize_entities(\n                client=client,\n                query=query,\n                api_key=api_key,\n                entity_api_url=entity_api_url,\n            )\n            recognized_count = len(recognized_tags)\n            result[\"recognized_entity_count\"] = recognized_count\n            if recognized_count > DIRECT_QUERY_ENTITY_LIMIT:\n                if not indicators or not indicators.strip():\n                    result[\"error\"] = (\n                        \"多实体查数（识别实体数 > 5）缺少 --indicators，\"\n                        \"请从 query 中提取金融指标后传入，用于构造「选定实体的{indicators}」\"\n                    )\n                    return result\n                entity_tags = recognized_tags\n                result[\"use_entity_tags\"] = True\n                search_query = _build_multi_entity_query(indicators)\n                result[\"indicators\"] = indicators.strip()\n                result[\"search_query\"] = search_query\n            else:\n                result[\"use_entity_tags\"] = False\n                search_query = query\n                if indicators and indicators.strip():\n                    result[\"indicators\"] = indicators.strip()\n            body = _build_request_body(search_query, entity_tags=entity_tags)\n            resp = await client.post(\n                url,\n                json=body,\n                headers={\n                    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n                    \"em_api_key\": api_key,\n                },\n            )\n```\n\nThe entity-recognition request similarly sends the credential to the supplied endpoint:\n\n```python\nresp = await client.post(\n    entity_api_url,\n    json={\"content\": query, \"typeCodes\": \"002,006005,006006,006007,006001,006002,006009,006010,006011,006012,005101,005201,005202,005203,005204,016,001001,001002,003007,003005,003002,003003,003008,003006,003004,003001,003200,003100,007,008,004,010,003300,003400,003500,003600,003700\"},\n    headers={\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n        \"em_api_key\": api_key,\n    },\n)\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe public query function accepts `api_base` and `entity_api_base` values without validating their schemes or hostnames. Both destinations receive the `EM_API_KEY` header. Consequently, a caller that can influence either argument can direct a credential-bearing HTTP request to an arbitrary server.\n\nThis is particularly relevant when the module is imported by another application that derives these arguments from configuration, request data, plugin input, or another insufficiently trusted source. Although the command-line interface does not expose these override parameters, the Python API does.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An application imports and calls `query_mx_finance_data`.\n2. The application permits an attacker to influence `api_base` or `entity_api_base`, directly or through configuration injection.\n3. The attacker supplies a controlled URL, such as `https://attacker.example/collect`.\n4. The Skill sends a POST request to that URL.\n5. The request contains `EM_API_KEY` in the `em_api_key` header.\n6. The attacker records the credential and associated query data.\n7. The attacker reuses the key against East Money APIs within the permissions and limits assigned to that key.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation can disclose:\n\n- The `EM_API_KEY` credential.\n- User-supplied financial queries.\n- Entity-recognition or search request data.\n- Entity metadata included in multi-entity requests.\n\nThe attacker obtains no direct local operating-system privileges from this flaw. However, the stolen key may permit unauthorized API requests, consume the victim's quota, access data available to the victim's account, or incur account-level consequences within the key's authorized scope.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Remove endpoint override parameters from production-facing APIs if they are only needed for testing.\n2. If overrides are required, parse each URL and require:\n   - The `https` scheme.\n   - An exact allowlisted hostname.\n   - An approved port.\n   - No embedded username or password.\n3. Maintain separate clients or request functions for trusted authenticated endpoints and unauthenticated custom endpoints.\n4. Never attach `EM_API_KEY` to a destination that has not passed validation.\n5. Keep redirects disabled for credential-bearing requests, and explicitly set `follow_redirects=False` to make the security assumption clear.\n6. Add tests confirming that HTTP URLs, unknown hosts, lookalike domains, embedded credentials, and malformed URLs are rejected.\n7. Prefer dependency injection of a mocked `httpx` transport for tests rather than changing production endpoint URLs.\n8. Rotate `EM_API_KEY` if there is evidence that an untrusted endpoint override has already been used.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T08","level":"note","message":{"text":"Unpinned Third-Party Dependencies Create a Supply-Chain Risk"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":111,"endLine":111}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"0ebb92bec5ca9f15"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, line 111  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned Third-Party Dependencies  \n**Risk Level**: Low  \n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```bash\npip3 install httpx pandas openpyxl --user\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe installation instructions request the latest versions of `httpx`, `pandas`, and `openpyxl` available from the configured Python package index. No version constraints, lock file, or package hashes are supplied.\n\nAs a result, installations are not reproducible and the reviewed source does not fully determine the code that will execute at installation and runtime. A future malicious, compromised, or incompatible package release could be installed without an additional review of this Skill.\n\nThe documented package names are established packages and no typosquatting or dependency-confusion package was identified. The finding concerns the absence of version and integrity controls rather than evidence that the currently named packages are malicious.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user follows the documented installation command.\n2. `pip` resolves the packages using the user's configured package index and selects currently available versions.\n3. A selected release or its distribution infrastructure is compromised, or the configured index serves a substituted artifact.\n4. The unverified package is downloaded and installed into the user's environment.\n5. Package installation or subsequent import executes attacker-controlled code with the privileges of the user running the command.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA compromised dependency could execute code with the installing user's privileges. Depending on that user's environment, this could expose files, environment variables such as `EM_API_KEY`, financial query results, and other credentials accessible to the process.\n\nThe practical likelihood is reduced because the instructions name well-known packages and do not request elevated installation privileges. The `--user` option also limits installation to the current user's Python environment rather than requiring system-wide administrative access.\n]]>","severity":"Low"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Create a reviewed requirements or lock file containing exact dependency versions.\n2. Generate and record cryptographic hashes for all approved distributions.\n3. Install dependencies with integrity enforcement, for example:\n\n```bash\npython3 -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n4. Specify the trusted package index explicitly in deployment documentation.\n5. Use an isolated virtual environment rather than modifying the general user environment.\n6. Introduce automated dependency vulnerability and release monitoring.\n7. Review and update pinned versions through a controlled process rather than resolving new releases automatically during installation.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":65,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789172636.7705348,"endTime":1789172702.1948311}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"mx-finance-data","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v576d6xvrstppxe38g6hczmtax8e7jgm-6uGIvb/clawscan-skillspector-3207003598/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:55.774077+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":31,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":187,"executable":false,"size_bytes":6307,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/get_data.py","type":"python","lines":877,"executable":true,"size_bytes":34751,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-206cf1ce5c254485951685f0ab6a1ae3","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill requires environment access, outbound network access, and writes output files, but it does not declare an explicit tool scope or permissions boundary. This can cause an agent platform to grant broader capabilities than users expect, increasing the risk of unintended data access, exfiltration, or filesystem side effects during execution.","remediation":"Add explicit permission metadata such as allowed-tools/permissions that narrowly scopes environment-variable access to EM_API_KEY, limits network access to the Eastmoney API domains actually required, and restricts file writes to a designated output directory. Document these capabilities clearly so invocation and consent are bounded.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-c3b70230548a402fb48040305de8350e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill description is broadly worded as a general natural-language financial data query tool across many markets and use cases, without clear trigger constraints. In agent environments, this increases the chance of over-broad or unintended activation, which can lead to unnecessary transmission of user-provided financial queries and generation of files when the user did not explicitly request this skill.","remediation":"Tighten the skill description and invocation criteria so the skill activates only for clearly defined finance-data retrieval tasks. Add explicit trigger examples, exclusions, and required user intent signals before making network requests or writing result files.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-8e2dc69876e3490aa70b0dfd05e6a444","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"The primary title and operational instructions are presented as a Chinese-only user-facing skill description, while the file does not explicitly offer the user a language choice or explain that the skill is limited to Chinese-language operation for compliance or regional reasons. This may violate language/locale policy if users are not given an opt-in or alternative locale behavior.","remediation":"Document supported languages explicitly and offer a user language choice where possible. If the skill is intended only for Chinese-language use due to provider or market constraints, state that limitation clearly and justify it in the description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-ba810be5371f4359996807a1a4cb4cdc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"scripts/get_data.py","start_line":2,"end_line":8},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring and all user-facing CLI descriptions are written solely in Chinese, indicating the skill is designed around a fixed language/locale without any opt-in or alternative. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user choice is a natural-language policy violation unless clearly justified as region-specific.","remediation":"Document that the skill is explicitly region/language-specific and why, or add user-selectable language support for prompts, messages, and output descriptions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/get_data.py","start_line":2,"end_line":8}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":8449,"completion_tokens":285,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":8734},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":12195,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":12209},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3816,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3830},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":12126,"completion_tokens":151,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":12277},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3747,"completion_tokens":347,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"t